## Data and APIs (Proposed)
- Tables (additive, with RLS): `video_metrics`, `comparable_baselines`, `experiments`, `goals` (or reuse `channel_strategy`), `competitors`.
- APIs:
  - `GET /api/dashboard/kpis` → baselines, thresholds, verdicts.
  - `GET /api/latest-video` → latest snapshot for channel; `POST /api/latest-video` forces refresh.
  - `GET /api/channel-recent-videos` → last 10 public uploads with stats.
  - `GET /api/latest-video-insights` → per-video retention samples + transcript-based insights.
  - `POST /api/experiments` / `PATCH /api/experiments/:id` → backlog + outcomes.
  - `GET/POST /api/goals` → goal weights.
  - `GET/POST /api/competitors` → competitor set, public stats.

## Prompting and Grounding
- Only pass numerics and facts from APIs; include confidence and window (T+1h/24h/7d).
- LLM output limited to: 1) verdict explanation (2–3 sentences), 2) next experiment with concrete steps, 3) 2–3 alternates (titles or hook fixes) if lever == CTR/retention.

## UX Notes
- Show confidence badges (low/med/high) based on sample size, variance, recency.
- One primary experiment per upload to reduce confounds.
- Respect reduced-motion; avoid auto-animated charts for accessibility.

